3. THE euftf ANOMALY — which construct does the model appear to answer?
==============================================================================
  the model's euftf country means correlate with HUMAN euftf at -0.2314

  most positively correlated human items:
    stflife    +0.6370
    happy      +0.6057
    hmsfmlsh   +0.5564
    trstplc    +0.5422
    trstlgl    +0.5343
  most negatively correlated human items:
    hincfel    -0.5726
    freehms    -0.4859
    health     -0.4548
    hmsacld    -0.4266
    polintr    -0.4013

  Read this as a hypothesis generator, not a test. euftf is a
  bipolar item whose numeric direction is a convention (0 = unification
  has gone too far, 10 = should go further), so an inverted reading is
  possible without the item being reverse-coded in the ESS sense. If the
  model's euftf tracks a substantively adjacent human item more strongly
  than it tracks human euftf, that is the substantive explanation the
  revision plan asks for, and it should be stated as one item's
  interpretation rather than generalised.

